Firstly, naturopathy is based on the principle of "vis medicatrix naturae," which means "the healing power of nature." This approach recognizes that the human body has an inherent ability to heal itself, and naturopaths work with patients to identify and address the underlying causes of illness, rather than just treating symptoms. This holistic approach can lead to more effective and sustainable health outcomes.

Secondly, naturopathy has a strong evidence base, with many studies demonstrating its effectiveness in treating a range of conditions, from chronic diseases like diabetes and hypertension to mental health conditions like anxiety and depression. For example, a 2018 systematic review published in the Journal of Alternative and Complementary Medicine found that naturopathic care was associated with significant improvements in blood sugar control and cardiovascular risk factors in patients with type 2 diabetes.

