Firstly, MOOCs have the potential to reach a much broader audience, including those who may not have had access to traditional higher education due to geographical, financial, or socio-economic constraints. This democratization of education can lead to a more diverse and inclusive learning environment, where students from all walks of life can participate and benefit from high-quality educational content.

