Thirdly, personalized medicine can also help reduce healthcare costs by reducing the need for trial-and-error approaches, which can lead to unnecessary tests, procedures, and medications. By using genetic information and other biomarkers, healthcare providers can make more informed decisions about treatment, which can lead to cost savings and improved resource allocation.

